.TH garuda-toolbox-queue-add 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-add \- Queue a change instead of carrying it out now. Type the change as its own command
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox queue add\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fICHANGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue a change instead of carrying it out now. Type the change as its own command
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICHANGE\fR>
The change as its own command takes it, for example `toggle on pipewire\-support`. Only changes the window queues fit: switches, apps, kernels, services at boot and masks, locales, accounts, groups, boot settings, drivers, DKMS builds and maintenance tasks
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox queue add toggle on pipewire\-support
  garuda\-toolbox queue add services enable sshd.service
  garuda\-toolbox queue add users lock guest
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-queue(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
